› how do I run the database.initialize?


• I’m going to give you the exact one-liner. database.initialize() is a Python method, not a
  standalone command, so you run it from a short python3 -c invocation against the SQLite file
  you want to repair.

• Run it from Python against the database file:

  python3 -c "from src.lib.database import Database; db = Database('data/asana.sqlite'); conn =
  db.connect(); db.initialize(conn); conn.close()"